IMPORT prelude

-- Legislation Act 2003 (Commonwealth), Chapter 2 Part 3: authorised versions and judicial notice (sections 15Z to 15ZB).
-- Text: C2004A01224.txt, compilation C2019C00084; it is not the authorised text.
-- Same conventions as lga-register.l4: JUST TRUE (the text says yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no), NOTHING (the text does not say).
-- The rules and the website that decide "in a format prescribed by the rules" and "in a way prescribed by the rules" are not among the sources: whether the format or the indication meets the rules is a plain input.

§ `Section 15Z: the documents this Part applies to`

DECLARE `Document for section 15Z` IS ONE OF
    `a registered Act`
    `a registered legislative instrument or notifiable instrument`
    `a registered explanatory statement for a legislative instrument`
    `a registered compilation of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument`
    `any other document for section 15Z`

-- "applies in relation to each of the following documents": a list not closed with "only", so another document is NOTHING.
-- src:632 | This Part applies in relation to each of the following documents (a registered law or explanatory statement) and, in the same way, to a provision or part of each document:
-- src:633 | (a) a registered Act;
-- src:634 | (b) a registered legislative instrument or notifiable instrument;
-- src:635 | (c) a registered explanatory statement for a legislative instrument;
-- src:636 | (d) a registered compilation of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument.
@ref s 15Z (src:632-636)
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Document for section 15Z`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15Z: this Part applies in relation to the document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the document`
    WHEN `a registered Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a registered legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a registered explanatory statement for a legislative instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a registered compilation of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any other document for section 15Z` THEN NOTHING

§ `Section 15ZA: authorised versions`

-- src:640 | (1) An electronic copy of a registered law or explanatory statement is an authorised version of the registered law or explanatory statement if:
-- src:641 | (a) the electronic copy is accessed at, or downloaded from, an approved website in a format prescribed by the rules; and
-- src:642 | (b) either:
-- src:643 | (i) the website indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that such a copy is an authorised version; or
-- src:644 | (ii) the electronic copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version.
-- src:645 | Example: For paragraph (a), a locked pdf file may be a format prescribed by the rules.
@ref s 15ZA(1) (src:640-645)
GIVEN `it is an electronic copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is accessed at, or downloaded from, an approved website in a format prescribed by the rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the website indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that such a copy is an authorised version` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the electronic copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15ZA(1): the electronic copy is an authorised version` MEANS
        `it is an electronic copy`
    AND `it is accessed at, or downloaded from, an approved website in a format prescribed by the rules`
    AND (`the website indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that such a copy is an authorised version` OR `the electronic copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version`)

-- src:646 | (2) An electronic copy of a registered law or explanatory statement is an authorised version of the registered law or explanatory statement if:
-- src:647 | (a) it is in a format prescribed by the rules; and
-- src:648 | (b) the electronic copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version.
-- src:649 | Example: For paragraph (a), a locked pdf file may be a format prescribed by the rules.
@ref s 15ZA(2) (src:646-649)
GIVEN `it is an electronic copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in a format prescribed by the rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the electronic copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15ZA(2): the electronic copy is an authorised version` MEANS
    `it is an electronic copy` AND `it is in a format prescribed by the rules` AND `the electronic copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version`

-- src:651 | (3) A printed copy of a registered law or explanatory statement is an authorised version of the registered law or explanatory statement if the copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version.
@ref s 15ZA(3) (src:651-651)
GIVEN `it is a printed copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15ZA(3): the printed copy is an authorised version` MEANS
    `it is a printed copy` AND `the copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version`

-- src:652 | (4) A printed copy of a registered law or explanatory statement is an authorised version of the registered law or explanatory statement if the copy is produced directly from another version of the registered law or explanatory statement that is an authorised version under subsection (1), (2) or (3), or this subsection.
@ref s 15ZA(4) (src:652-652)
GIVEN `it is a printed copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is produced directly from another version that is an authorised version under subsection (1), (2) or (3), or this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15ZA(4): the printed copy is an authorised version` MEANS
    `it is a printed copy` AND `it is produced directly from another version that is an authorised version under subsection (1), (2) or (3), or this subsection`

-- Subsections (1) to (4) each say "is an authorised version ... if": a copy that meets none of them answers JUST FALSE (the 2026-11-04 ruling on "if"); a copy that meets one is JUST TRUE.
-- src:640 | (1) An electronic copy of a registered law or explanatory statement is an authorised version of the registered law or explanatory statement if:
-- src:641 | (a) the electronic copy is accessed at, or downloaded from, an approved website in a format prescribed by the rules; and
-- src:642 | (b) either:
-- src:643 | (i) the website indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that such a copy is an authorised version; or
-- src:644 | (ii) the electronic copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version.
-- src:645 | Example: For paragraph (a), a locked pdf file may be a format prescribed by the rules.
-- src:646 | (2) An electronic copy of a registered law or explanatory statement is an authorised version of the registered law or explanatory statement if:
-- src:647 | (a) it is in a format prescribed by the rules; and
-- src:648 | (b) the electronic copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version.
-- src:649 | Example: For paragraph (a), a locked pdf file may be a format prescribed by the rules.
-- src:650 | Authorised printed versions
-- src:651 | (3) A printed copy of a registered law or explanatory statement is an authorised version of the registered law or explanatory statement if the copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version.
-- src:652 | (4) A printed copy of a registered law or explanatory statement is an authorised version of the registered law or explanatory statement if the copy is produced directly from another version of the registered law or explanatory statement that is an authorised version under subsection (1), (2) or (3), or this subsection.
@ref s 15ZA(1) to (4) (src:640-652)
GIVEN `it is an electronic copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a printed copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is accessed at, or downloaded from, an approved website in a format prescribed by the rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the website indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that such a copy is an authorised version` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in a format prescribed by the rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is produced directly from another version that is an authorised version under subsection (1), (2) or (3), or this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15ZA: the copy of the registered law or explanatory statement is an authorised version` MEANS
    IF    `s 15ZA(1): the electronic copy is an authorised version` `it is an electronic copy` `it is accessed at, or downloaded from, an approved website in a format prescribed by the rules` `the website indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that such a copy is an authorised version` `the copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version`
       OR `s 15ZA(2): the electronic copy is an authorised version` `it is an electronic copy` `it is in a format prescribed by the rules` `the copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version`
       OR `s 15ZA(3): the printed copy is an authorised version` `it is a printed copy` `the copy indicates, in a way prescribed by the rules, that it is an authorised version`
       OR `s 15ZA(4): the printed copy is an authorised version` `it is a printed copy` `it is produced directly from another version that is an authorised version under subsection (1), (2) or (3), or this subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Presumption in section 15ZA(5)` IS ONE OF
    `(a): a website purporting to be an approved website is an approved website`
    `(b): if accessed at such a website, the thing is registered`
    `(c): an electronic copy accessed at or downloaded from an approved website is an authorised version under subsection (1)`
    `(d): an electronic copy is an authorised version under subsection (2)`
    `(e): a printed copy is an authorised version under subsection (3) or (4)`
    `(f): an authorised version of a registered Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, as made, correctly shows the text as made`
    `(g): an authorised version of a registered explanatory statement correctly shows the text as approved by the rule-maker`
    `(h): subject to subsection 15Q(4), an authorised version of a registered compilation correctly shows the text as amended (if at all) and in force on the compilation date`

-- "It is presumed, unless the contrary is proved": the contrary proved answers JUST FALSE; the facts the paragraph speaks of not holding is outside the presumption, so NOTHING.
-- Paragraph (h) is "subject to subsection 15Q(4)": for an amendment with retrospective commencement that 15Q(4) does not require a compilation to show, the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:654 | (5) It is presumed, unless the contrary is proved, that:
-- src:655 | (a) a website purporting to be an approved website is an approved website; and
-- src:656 | (b) if accessed at a website mentioned in paragraph (a), an Act, a legislative instrument, a notifiable instrument, an explanatory statement for a legislative instrument or a compilation of an Act or a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument is registered; and
-- src:657 | (c) an electronic copy of a registered law or explanatory statement accessed at, or downloaded from, an approved website is an authorised version under subsection (1), if:
-- src:658 | (i) the website indicates (in any way) that such a copy is an authorised version; or
-- src:659 | (ii) the copy indicates (in any way) that the copy is an authorised version; and
-- src:660 | (d) an electronic copy of a registered law or explanatory statement is an authorised version under subsection (2) if the copy indicates (in any way) that it is an authorised version; and
-- src:661 | (e) a printed copy of a registered law or explanatory statement is an authorised version under subsection (3) or (4) if the copy indicates (in any way) that it is an authorised version; and
-- src:662 | (f) an authorised version of a registered Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, as made, correctly shows the text of the Act or instrument as made; and
-- src:663 | (g) an authorised version of a registered explanatory statement for a legislative instrument correctly shows the text of the statement as approved by the rule-maker (under subsection 15J(2) or (3)); and
-- src:664 | (h) subject to subsection 15Q(4), an authorised version of a registered compilation of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument correctly shows the text of the Act or instrument as amended (if at all) and in force on the compilation date.
@ref s 15ZA(5) (src:654-664)
GIVEN `the presumption` IS A `Presumption in section 15ZA(5)`
      `the facts the paragraph speaks of hold` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is an amendment with retrospective commencement that subsection 15Q(4) does not require the compilation to take account of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15ZA(5): the presumption holds` MEANS
    IF NOT `the facts the paragraph speaks of hold` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF `the contrary is proved`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE
            CONSIDER `the presumption`
            WHEN `(h): subject to subsection 15Q(4), an authorised version of a registered compilation correctly shows the text as amended (if at all) and in force on the compilation date` THEN
                (IF `the matter is an amendment with retrospective commencement that subsection 15Q(4) does not require the compilation to take account of` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE)
            WHEN `(a): a website purporting to be an approved website is an approved website` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `(b): if accessed at such a website, the thing is registered` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `(c): an electronic copy accessed at or downloaded from an approved website is an authorised version under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `(d): an electronic copy is an authorised version under subsection (2)` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `(e): a printed copy is an authorised version under subsection (3) or (4)` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `(f): an authorised version of a registered Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, as made, correctly shows the text as made` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `(g): an authorised version of a registered explanatory statement correctly shows the text as approved by the rule-maker` THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:666 | (6) A way of indicating that is prescribed by rules made for the purposes of subsection (1), (2) or (3), or an indication mentioned in paragraph (5)(c), (d) or (e), may include an indication consisting of any text, including one or more of the following:
-- src:667 | (a) a logo;
-- src:668 | (b) a form of words;
-- src:669 | (c) a unique identifier, for a registered law or explanatory statement, prescribed by the rules.
@ref s 15ZA(6) (src:666-669)
GIVEN `the indication consists of text, including a logo, a form of words or a unique identifier prescribed by the rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15ZA(6): the way of indicating may include the indication` MEANS
    IF `the indication consists of text, including a logo, a form of words or a unique identifier prescribed by the rules` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 15ZB: judicial notice`

DECLARE `Matter for section 15ZB(1)` IS ONE OF
    `(a): the assent, and the day of assent, of an Act`
    `(b): the making, and the day of making, of a registered legislative instrument or notifiable instrument`
    `(c): the text of a registered law or explanatory statement`
    `(d): the registration, and day of registration, of a registered law or explanatory statement`
    `(e): the commencement of a registered Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, or any provision of one`
    `(f): editorial changes made in preparing a registered compilation`
    `(g): the text and compilation date of a registered compilation`
    `(h): whether a copy of a registered law or explanatory statement is an authorised version`
    `any other matter`

-- jural: immunity of a party to the proceedings from having to prove the matter | disability of the court or tribunal to require proof
-- "any of the following" is a list not closed with "only", so another matter is NOTHING.
-- src:671 | (1) In proceedings in a court or tribunal, proof is not required about any of the following:
-- src:672 | (a) the assent, and the day of assent, of an Act;
-- src:673 | (b) the making, and the day of making, of a registered legislative instrument or notifiable instrument;
-- src:674 | (c) the text of a registered law or explanatory statement;
-- src:675 | (d) the registration, and day of registration, of a registered law or explanatory statement;
-- src:676 | (e) the commencement of a registered Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, or any provision of a registered Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument;
-- src:677 | (f) editorial changes made to an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument in preparing a registered compilation of the Act or instrument;
-- src:678 | (g) the text and compilation date of a registered compilation of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument;
-- src:679 | (h) whether a copy of a registered law or explanatory statement is an authorised version of the registered law or explanatory statement.
@ref s 15ZB(1) (src:671-679)
GIVEN `the matter arises in proceedings in a court or tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter` IS A `Matter for section 15ZB(1)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15ZB(1): proof is not required about the matter` MEANS
    IF `the matter arises in proceedings in a court or tribunal`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the matter`
        WHEN `any other matter` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `(a): the assent, and the day of assent, of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `(b): the making, and the day of making, of a registered legislative instrument or notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `(c): the text of a registered law or explanatory statement` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `(d): the registration, and day of registration, of a registered law or explanatory statement` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `(e): the commencement of a registered Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, or any provision of one` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `(f): editorial changes made in preparing a registered compilation` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `(g): the text and compilation date of a registered compilation` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `(h): whether a copy of a registered law or explanatory statement is an authorised version` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: privilege of the court or tribunal | no-right of a party to insist on a particular source
-- src:680 | (2) A court or tribunal may inform itself of anything mentioned in subsection (1) in any way it considers appropriate.
@ref s 15ZB(2) (src:680-680)
GIVEN `the court or tribunal informs itself of a matter mentioned in subsection (1) in a way it considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15ZB(2): the court or tribunal may inform itself in that way` MEANS
    IF `the court or tribunal informs itself of a matter mentioned in subsection (1) in a way it considers appropriate` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- jural: claim of the parties | duty of the court or tribunal
-- src:681 | (3) However, the court or tribunal must consider whether the source it intends to use appears to be a reliable source of information.
@ref s 15ZB(3) (src:681-681)
GIVEN `the court or tribunal intends to use a source for a matter mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15ZB(3): the court or tribunal must consider whether the source appears to be a reliable source of information` MEANS
    IF `the court or tribunal intends to use a source for a matter mentioned in subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- "For the purposes of subsection (3), an authorised version ... is, subject to subsection 15Q(4), a reliable source": a copy that is not an authorised version is outside the words, so NOTHING.
-- src:682 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3), an authorised version of a registered law or explanatory statement is, subject to subsection 15Q(4), a reliable source of information.
@ref s 15ZB(4) (src:682-682)
GIVEN `the copy is an authorised version of a registered law or explanatory statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is an amendment with retrospective commencement that subsection 15Q(4) does not require a compilation to take account of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15ZB(4): the authorised version is a reliable source of information` MEANS
    IF `the copy is an authorised version of a registered law or explanatory statement` AND NOT `the matter is an amendment with retrospective commencement that subsection 15Q(4) does not require a compilation to take account of`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:683 | (5) This section does not limit any other law providing how a court or tribunal may be informed about a matter mentioned in subsection (1).
@ref s 15ZB(5) (src:683-683)
GIVEN `another law provides how a court or tribunal may be informed about a matter mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15ZB(5): this section limits the other law` MEANS
    IF `another law provides how a court or tribunal may be informed about a matter mentioned in subsection (1)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
